-- "trở lên", "kéo dài" = at least; "trở xuống" = at most; "dưới", "ít hơn", "nhỏ hơn" = less
-- than; "lớn hơn", "hơn", "trên", "sau tuần thứ" = more than; "trong vòng", "trong thời
-- gian" = at most) and the number from its digits (Vietnamese format: a dot before three
-- digits groups thousands, a dot or comma before one or two digits is a decimal point), and
-- computes the expected answer from that reading. A phrase with no comparator word is marked
-- HAND-READ below, and for it the expectation is the encoder's reading. Two values per
-- threshold: on it, and one step past it. Every other threshold of the condition is set to
-- a passing value (or, inside an "or", to a failing one), so the answer turns on this one.

